@PerpsPadfun is a Solana launchpad where every coin is backed by a live leveraged perp. Launch a coin on a @MeteoraAG curve, or route a pumpfun coin's creator fees in, and pick what backs it: 2x to 40x, long or short, on crypto, tokenized stocks or commodities.

Each coin gets a sub-wallet only the keeper controls. It claims the coin's trading fees every few seconds and splits them on the spot: half becomes USDC margin on a @PhoenixTrade perp via @ImperialPerps, 15% pays the creator, 20% goes to the platform treasury, 15% buys the coin back and burns it. Fees only ever add margin. When the position's gain climbs 25% past its last high, a fifth is closed and 70% of that profit is burned too. Nothing closes on a loss.

Two months in, the machine is running but almost empty. 114 coins are listed, 65 launched natively and 49 routed from @Pumpfun, most of them in a single week at the end of July. They have traded $8.6M in total, and solana:PerPsCe2SJ7Q25CN4R5TTX4fmBdmknE2hQmqCt96fHL is 83% of it. That volume has produced about $161K in fees, of which $113K went into perp collateral, $55K into buybacks and $32K to the treasury. Today the perp side holds $77K of open interest on $14K of collateral, and two coins, solana:PerPsCe2SJ7Q25CN4R5TTX4fmBdmknE2hQmqCt96fHL and $LONGCAT, account for 88% of every perp fill ever routed. The one number that looks large is solana:PerPsCe2SJ7Q25CN4R5TTX4fmBdmknE2hQmqCt96fHL's burn: 266M tokens, 27% of supply, gone.

